\details{
Pass original-scale knot positions (including the domain ends), or an
integer \code{k} and \code{region}. \code{k} matches BayesGP's equally spaced cubic basis
(\code{nbasis = k}, \code{norder = 4}), which uses \code{k - 2} breakpoints.

The prior density uses adlaplace's \code{random_mult} kernel with a fixed
precision \code{Q} (one SD theta). Use \code{\link[adlaplace:psd]{adlaplace::psd()}} /
\code{\link[adlaplace:psd_prior]{adlaplace::psd_prior()}} for a PC prior on the predictive SD. The predictive
SD does not depend on location. For \code{m > 1} it is the SD of the sum of
independent harmonics.

FEM construction follows Ziang Zhang's BayesGP seasonal B-splines
(arXiv:2305.09914), with Gauss-Legendre quadrature and
\code{\link[splines:splineDesign]{splines::splineDesign()}} (no \strong{fda} dependency at runtime).
